  55:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * Function Name: Cy_BLE_Start
  56:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** ***************************************************************************//**
  57:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  58:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  This function initializes the BLE Stack which consists of the BLE Stack 
  59:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  Manager, BLE Controller, and BLE Host modules. It takes care of initializing
  60:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  the Profile layer, schedulers, Timer and other platform-related
  61:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  resources required for the BLE component. It also registers the callback 
  62:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  function for BLE events that will be registered in the BLE stack.
  63:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  64:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  Note that this function does not reset the BLE Stack.
  65:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  66:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  For the HCI-Mode of operation, this function will not initialize the BLE Host 
  67:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  module.
  68:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  69:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  Calling this function results in generation of a CY_BLE_EVT_STACK_ON event
  70:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  on successful initialization of the BLE Stack.
  71:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *
  72:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  In the Dual Core mode, this function should be called on both cores in the 
  73:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  following sequence:
  74:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *   - call this function on CM0+ core to initialize the Controller.
  75:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *   - start CM4 core by calling Cy_SysEnableCM4() function.
  76:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *   - call this function on CM4 core to initialize the Host and Profiles.
  77:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  78:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  \param callbackFunc: Event callback function to receive events from BLE stack.
  79:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *   cy_ble_callback_t is a function pointer type.
  80:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  81:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * \return
  82:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  cy_en_ble_api_result_t : Return value indicates if the function succeeded or 
  83:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  failed. The following are possible error codes.
  84:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** * 
  85:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *   <table>
  86:Generated_Source\PSoC6/BLE.c **** *  	  <tr>
